# Git commits

When creating commits or pushing:

- Use a **very short**, natural commit message (a few words). Write like a human teammate, not a changelog bot.
- Prefer lowercase or sentence case; no buzzwords, no "comprehensive", "finalize", "enhance", "refactor to improve", or essay-style subjects.
- One line only. No body unless the user asks.
- Never add `Co-authored-by: Cursor`, `Made-with: Cursor`, or any AI attribution trailer.
- Only commit when the user asks. Only push when the user asks.
- Do not rewrite history unless the user explicitly asks.

## Good

- `init scaffold`
- `update architecture`
- `fix ehr mock`
- `add rules config`

## Bad

- `Scaffold FA5-aligned project layout with service stubs and configs.`
- `Add finalized end-to-end architecture diagram and SSoT link.`
- `Update documentation to reflect the new agent orchestration flow.`
